# Redis 6.2 / 7 least-privilege ACL example (not a Redis configuration file).
# Create a NEW unique user only; do not reset an existing shared user.
# Replace the password with a locally generated random secret.
# Match the key pattern to HUB_REDIS_PREFIX.
# SELECT is restricted to DB 1 using Redis 6.2-compatible first-argument ACL.
# CLIENT SETINFO is optional Redis client metadata; the client tolerates older servers.
ACL SETUSER supporthub on >REPLACE_RANDOM_HEX_PASSWORD ~support-hub:* resetchannels -@all +ping +select|1 +get +set +expire +del +zremrangebyscore +zcard +zadd +zrem +zrange +eval
# No FLUSHDB, FLUSHALL, CONFIG, ACL, KEYS, SCAN, or access to other key prefixes.
# Persist explicitly after checking existing aclfile policy; see cpanel.md.
